{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** Version 3 fixes the latest-upstream proof and makes the parser a triage tool. Three gaps remain in §4. Uncertainty can become a failure, a linked double refusal can become inconclusive, and a forecast outside the H5 sample can still supply the apparent improvement.\n\n### Blocking changes\n\n1. **Give P three outcomes per pair.** Suppose 60 dates are jointly readable, the control has five definite contradictions and the linked arm has zero. On the other 13 dates, the control is clear and the linked forecast is unresolved. Both improvement and no improvement are possible. The current rule returns **fail**. Bound the difference in definite days over all 73 dates in both directions, retaining known classes on dates where only one arm is readable. Call a pair improved when even the least favourable completion improves, failed when even the most favourable completion cannot improve, and inconclusive when the unresolved dates could change the result. State explicitly whether the two-day control floor uses jointly readable dates. [Primary rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:78) · [Verdict precedence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:109)\n\n2. **Separate product failure from infrastructure failure.** H1 calls a linked double refusal harm, but verdict step 1 makes any stop inconclusive. Production returns `judgement_refused_twice` and stops the day, so both rules apply to the same event. Make a confirmed linked double refusal fail and a control double refusal invalidate the comparison. Reserve the infrastructure outcome for budget, transport, and harness stops. For the rate check, count attempted reader judgements, including terminal refusals, and use matched reader-days for the paired rate. Report propagation-only refusals separately so extra clean judgement days cannot dilute the comparison. [H1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:86) · [Product refusal path](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:83)\n\n3. **Make decisive gains traceable beyond the seven H5 dates.** Keep the seven-date sample for H5’s comparative threshold. Also review the arithmetic and sourcing of every distinct linked answer that supplies a gain needed to pass P. Otherwise, an unsupported `v9` forecast between sample dates can carry the verdict. Preserve the actual forecast class separately from its eligibility for credit. If an unsupported CPU increment can be quantified, show the comparison without it. If its size is unresolved and it could decide P, withhold the pass. For H3, trigger review when a claim’s **amount, scope, or attribution** changes. An unchanged $393B can shift from company consensus to segment consensus. Use the paired control’s accepted conclusion in force on that date when it has no fresh judgement, and compare the specific grounding error. [H3–H5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:93) · [July arithmetic and sourcing rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md:5)\n\n### Thresholds and reading load\n\n- **60 of 73** is defensible as a coverage policy. It is **82.2%**, while the previous 80% rule would require **59** dates. State that 60 deliberately allows at most 13 unreadable dates. The two-sided bounds above should determine whether those missing dates matter.\n- **H1’s 5 points and 3 refusals** need an explicit tolerance rationale. With 266 linked judgements and zero control refusals, 13 linked refusals would still clear the gate. At this workload, the five-point rule already implies more than three additional refusals. **H5’s two extra failures** is a defensible tolerance for the fixed 14 question-dates per sequence once a single material error cannot supply the primary gain. Both are product tolerances to freeze before seeing results. [Thresholds](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:86) · [Workload basis](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:118)\n\nI counted **72 distinct v9/v14 answer pairs** on old-2’s 73 dates. Budget up to **438 pair classifications** across six sequences, about **213 linked v14 reviews** on the stored schedule, and **168 first and second H5 marks** before adjudication. The workload is feasible, but the protocol is incomplete. Before launch, pin a worksheet keyed by judgement IDs and date spans. Give readers the full forecast text, the endpoints and excerpt to record, and the exact request and dated sources for harm checks. Apply source-backed adjudication to verdict-changing disagreements in P, H3 and H4 as well as H5. The old-1 September 8 case, **$419B against $414–421B**, is a useful worked example of overlap. The roughly three-hour estimate covers the model run. Reader time needs its own estimate. [Hand-reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:68) · [Overlap example](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/parser-validation.txt:35) · [Run time](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:126)"}}
